    {
      "case": "2618 relative receipt and open date",
      "source_ids": [
        "DCP-LETT-2618"
      ],
      "requirement": "Render the Sunday evening item with its relative date only: Darwin received Horner’s note and Lepsius memorandum “this morning,” learned of the work, and says he now knows where to look. That establishes receipt of the note/memorandum, not reading of the memorandum or a precise calendar day; preserve its open two-year date window and the absent memorandum. Verso biblical chronology remains a separate possible Horner layer.",
      "source_provenance": [
